  "description": "DEFINITION INTEGRALE FRAMESET\n\nThe latest evolution of our unique MASON Definition, tailored to optimise speedy handling and clean cable-free lines\n\nThe aluminium MASON Definition is our Fast Far bicycle for multi-surface road riding. Improved and updated to keep it ahead of the pack, the new Definition Integrale offers an alternative to the Definition3, with shortened chainstays, a new fork, and fully integrated routing that conceals cables and hoses within the cockpit of your bicycle.\n\nOptimised for electronic groupsets, our approach to integration has already transformed the titanium MASON Aspect. Now it’s time for the aluminium Definition to offer this streamlined, focussed Integrale option.\n\nNEW – Definition Integrale\n\nRefined geometry for sportier handling\n\nFully integrated routing\n\nOptimised for electronic shifting such as SRAM AXS and Shimano Di2\n\nMASON x Deda AR carbon fork\n\nAlternatively, the MASON Definition3 offers the same Dedacciai aluminium performance as the Definition Integrale, but with conventional internal routing and other additional features.\n\n50 Definition Integrale Launch Edition frames will be finished as shown, with individual numbering, special Launch Edition detailing and brass-finish head badge. Production models will feature a tungsten-finish headbadge and will not have individual numbers or Launch Edition decals.\n\nCustom Dedacciai aluminium frame, refined and reworked for performance riding\n\nLower crown height and stack height than Definition3, giving a sportier position with a fast, attacking feel\n\nProgressive geometry, keeping the handling confident, direct and comfortable across all sizes, in tune with rider height and build\n\n8 sizes for precise fit: 48 to 62cm\n\nOptimised for electronic shifting only\n\nFully compatible with full-length mudguards\n\n2 new finishes: ProcessWhite and PrismGreen",
